<title>USA: PP&amp;L Resources Inc Q1 shr $0.72 vs $0.73.</title>
<headline>PP&amp;L Resources Inc Q1 shr $0.72 vs $0.73.</headline>
<dateline>ALLENTOWN, Pa. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.72		    $0.73</p>
<p> Net			116,772		  116,260</p>
<p> Revs		     785,769		  789,192</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 163,192		  159,890</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.04		    $2.13</p>
<p> Net			329,944		  337,593</p>
<p> Revs		   2,906,820		2,813,506</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 161,879		  158,570</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q1 and rolling 12 month period reflects effects of weather.</p>
<p>After excluding the effects of weather, Q1 earnings per share would have been $0.76 a share, compared with $0.69 a share in last year's first quarter.</p>
<p>1997 rolling 12 month period reflects a reduction in bulk power sales to a New Jersey utility. This cut earnings per share by $0.09 for the period.</p>
</text>
